// expect-error: NITPICK-DERIVE-002
// expect-error: NITPICK-DERIVE-002
//
// `Default` AND `Display` WERE ON THE LIST OF NINE AND D-123 REMOVED BOTH. Their
// own code, not "unknown name": a reader who writes one is not making a typo, and
// a message that treats them as one sends somebody to check their spelling.
//
// `Default` would have the compiler choose values that carry meaning, and several
// obvious choices are false here — `fd` zero is stdin (D-042), `tbb32` zero claims
// "no error", a pointer zero is NULL. It reintroduces through an explicit door what
// D-010 removed: a value appearing that nobody chose.
//
// `Display` was a second name for `ToString`'s job.
mod:removed;

#[derive(Default)]
struct:A = { int32:x; };

#[derive(Display)]
struct:B = { int32:x; };

func:main = int32(cstring[]:_~argv) { exit 0i32; };
